  "operation": {
    "kind": "prompt",
    "user": "You are opening an exploration. Your job is to write the criteria the candidates\nwill be scored against — **before any candidate exists**. That order is the only\nreason the scores mean anything: criteria written after the options are criteria\nwritten to justify a favourite.\n\n## The constraint\n\n{{.inputs.constraint}}\n\n## What varies across candidates\n\n{{.inputs.varies}}\n\n## What a candidate is here, and how to shape one\n\n{{.inputs.guidance}}\n\n_Paths — open them with `read_file`._\n\n## Findings from the previous pass\n\n{{.inputs.prior_findings}}\n\nIf that is non-empty, this exploration is being re-opened because the critique\nsaid the approach itself was wrong — not the execution. Read the findings as a\nstatement that the earlier criteria missed something, and say in the brief what\nthey missed.\n\n## What to produce\n\n`brief` — the constraint restated in your own words, in a few sentences: what is\nactually being decided, what is fixed and may not be moved, and what the winning\ncandidate has to be true of. Where prior findings arrived, append what they\nchange.\n\n`criteria` — **3 to 6**, each with a `name`, a `weight` in 0..1 summing to\nroughly 1, and a `why`. Rules:\n\n- A criterion has to be able to **separate** candidates. \"Is good\" cannot. Prefer\n  one that names an observable: recoverability from a wrong choice, how much a\n  reader has to know before step 1, how many places a change lands.\n- Weight what actually matters here, not what is easy to score. A criterion\n  weighted 0.05 is one you did not need.\n- At least one criterion must be a **cost**: what building this takes, what it\n  forecloses, what it makes harder later. Explorations that score only benefits\n  always conclude that building is best.\n- Do not write a criterion that only one candidate could ever win. That is a\n  preference wearing a criterion's clothes.\n",
    "config": {
      "model": "claude-opus-5"
    },
    "input": {},
    "output": {
      "name": "output",
      "kind": "json",
      "schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "brief": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "criteria": {
            "type": "array",
            "minItems": 3,
            "maxItems": 6,
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": [
                "name",
                "weight"
              ],
              "properties": {
                "name": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "weight": {
                  "type": "number",
                  "minimum": 0,
                  "maximum": 1
                },
                "why": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "brief",
          "criteria"
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "environment": {
    "tools": [
      "read_file"
    ],
    "permissions": {
      "profile": "read-only",
      "tools": {
        "read_file": "allow"
      }
    }
  },
  "slotMeta": {
    "inputs.constraint": {
      "description": "What is being decided."
    },
    "inputs.guidance": {
      "description": "Paths to what shapes a candidate here. Read them with read_file."
    },
    "inputs.prior_findings": {
      "optional": true
    }
  }
}
